        "original_id": "260dbb05-9ee7-51a4-b553-4d800048353d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: David Lean, Madeleine Smith, Emile L'Angelier, Ann Todd, Dorothy Anne Todd\n- Works: Madeleine (1950 film)\n- Events: Madeleine Smith trial\n- Places: Glasgow\n\nFacts:\n- In 1857, Madeleine Smith, a young woman from a wealthy Glasgow family, was tried for the murder of her lover, Emile L'Angelier.\n- The Madeleine Smith trial was heavily publicized in contemporary newspapers and was labeled \"the trial of the century.\"\n- On 24 January 1909, Dorothy Anne Todd, known as Ann Todd, was born.\n- Madeleine is a 1950 film directed by David Lean and based on the true story of Madeleine Smith.\n- Ann Todd was an English actress and producer.\n- On 6 May 1993, Ann Todd died.",
